      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,{3}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={3}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({3}^{x})}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+{3}^{x}{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+{3}^{x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-{3}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
